  "body": "## What to build\n\nAdd the assembly geometry resolver that turns a component stack into a resolved `Tool`, gauge length, and `ToolBody`.\n\n1. Classify `MCS_INSERT` as `CsysRole::Mounting` in `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_csys.rs`.\n2. Implement forward kinematics in `crates/tools` (pure rigid-frame math) and `crates/app/src/tool_assembly.rs`:\n   - Start from the root component's machine-side `MCS` at identity.\n   - Chain each child's `MCS` onto its parent's `CSW*` port.\n   - Support an optional axial index angle (`z_rot_deg`) around the mating Z axis and an optional stickout `projection_mm` for cylindrical and collet mounts.\n3. Normalize the assembly to CamCraft's tool frame so the active cutting tip (`CIP` for spindle tools, `CRP` / nose centre for turning inserts) sits at `(0, 0, 0)`.\n   - Compute spindle gauge length as the `+Z` height of the root `MCS` origin in the normalized frame.\n   - Derive turning `orientation` (LinuxCNC 1–8) from holder approach angle, holder hand, and insert shape when not overridden.\n4. Derive the judged collision body (`ToolBody`) from all non-cutting components:\n   - Combine STEP/STL/OBJ meshes and parametric `SpunProfile` holders into one `HolderProfile` (spindle) or `LatheClearance` (lathe).\n   - Run size and tip-gap checks (`MAX_BODY_RADIUS`, `MAX_BODY_HEIGHT`, `MAX_TIP_GAP`) on the combined assembly, never on upper adapters alone.\n   - Allow turning assemblies with a separate insert component to build `LatheClearance` from the holder mesh without requiring a manual `InsertZone`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Depends on the component model sub-issue of #2452.\n- Does not block on #1039: turning STEP components use explicit stored frames until turning STEP auto-alignment lands.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests in `crates/tools` and `crates/app` pin derived `Tool` cutting parameters, gauge length, spindle `HolderProfile` bands, and lathe `LatheClearance` bands for multi-component assemblies.\n- Tests cover mixed parametric (`SpunProfile` / built-in holder) and STEP-mesh stacks, plus non-zero `z_rot_deg` indexing and `projection_mm` stickout.\n- Tests pin named refusals for missing frames, ambiguous ports, cycle links, non-finite transforms, and bodies reaching into flutes.\n\nPart of #2452\n",
